From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] aoc: port to android-mainline

One cumulative patch, kept in two sections: the 6.1 -> 6.18 port this
project first needed for GrapheneOS's 6.18 GKI, then 6.18 -> android-mainline.

== 6.1 -> 6.18 ==
(aoc: don't pull Laguna's arm-smmu-v3 module into gs201 builds)

aoc_core depends on //private/google-modules/iommu/arm-smmu-v3 for
pixel-iommu-fault.ko. Only Laguna adds that package's Kconfig
(lga_defconfig: ARM_SMMU_V3_PIXEL, GOOGLE_ACFW_DEBUG, ...); on gs201 the
symbols do not exist, the kernel_module builds none of its five declared
outs, and the lynx dist fails:

  ERROR: Unable to find acfw-debug.ko ... arm_smmu_v3.ko ...
         pixel-iommu-fault.ko in .../iommu/arm-smmu-v3

Depend on that module only for soc_is_laguna_or_later; keep the
header-only fault_headers everywhere. On gs201 the pixel_iommu_*() fault
API aoc.c calls is provided by samsung_iommu.ko (gs201_soc, which aoc_core
already depends on), so aoc.c itself is unchanged.

== 6.18 -> android-mainline ==

Linux 6.18 -> android-mainline (7.3):

  * of_node_to_fwnode() -> of_fwnode_handle(), snd_soc_component_get_dapm()
    -> snd_soc_component_to_dapm() (mechanical, as upstream).
  * usb/usb_hooks_impl_whi.c: android_rvh_usb_dev_suspend and
    android_vh_usb_dev_resume (and trace/hooks/usb.h) do not exist in
    android-mainline. Their registrations are fenced off; they kept a USB
    device awake while AOC offloads audio, which the Debian image does not
    use. The handlers stay, __maybe_unused.
---
